<tool id="ampvis2_alpha_diversity" name="ampvis2 alpha diversity" version="0.1.0+galaxy0" profile="22.09">
    <description>calculate alpha diversity indices</description>
    <macros/><xrefs>
        <xref type="bio.tools">ampvis2</xref>
    </xrefs>
    <requirements>
        <requirement type="package" version="1.4.0">r-cli</requirement>
    </requirements>
    <command detect_errors="exit_code">
Rscript '$__tool_directory__/ampvis2_alpha_diversity.R'
--input '${input}'
--output '${output}'
--index '${index}'
--rarefy '${rarefy}'
    </command>
    <inputs>
        <param name="input" type="data" format="rds" label="An ampvis2 RDS dataset"/>
        <param name="index" type="select" label="Alpha diversity index">
            <option value="shannon">Shannon entropy</option>
            <option value="simpson">Simpson's reciprocal</option>
            <option value="invsimpson">Inverse Simpson's reciprocal</option>
            <option value="pielou">Pielou's evenness</option>
            <option value="fisher">Fisher's alpha</option>
            <option value="menhinick">Menhinick's index</option>
            <option value="ace">ACE estimator</option>
            <option value="observed">Number of observed species</option>
        </param>
        <param name="rarefy" type="integer" min="1" value="1000" label="Rarefaction depth"/>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="output" format="tabular" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Alpha Diversity"/>
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <test>
            <param name="input" ftype="rds" value="alpha.rds"/>
            <param name="index" value="shannon"/>
            <param name="rarefy" value="1000"/>
            <output name="output" file="alpha_shannon.tabular" compare="sim_size"/>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help>
What it does
============

Calculate alpha-diversity indices for each sample and combines with the metadata.

The Galaxy tool calls the `amp_alpha_diversity
<https://kasperskytte.github.io/ampvis2/reference/amp_alphadiv.html>`_ function
of the ampvis2 package.

Usage
=====

The alpha-diversity indices are calculated per sample using the vegan function `diversity <https://rdrr.io/pkg/vegan/man/diversity.html>`_,
where the read abundances are first rarefied using `rrarefy <https://rdrr.io/pkg/vegan/man/rarefy.html>`_ by the size of the rarefy argument.
Refer to the vegan documentation for details about the different indices and how they are
calculated.


Input
=====


        An ampvis2 RDS dataset obtained by the ``ampvis2: load`` tool (or ``ampvis2: mergereplicates`` or one of the
        ``ampvis2: subset ...`` tools).


Output
======

A tabular dataset containing the chosen alpha-diversity measures per sample.
    </help>
    <citations>
        <citation type="doi">10.1038/s41597-021-00654-0</citation>
    </citations>
</tool>